1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
There are heroes. There are superheroes. And then there's Hancock.

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Hancock is a fantasy, action film directed by Peter Berg.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Hancock is a down-and-out superhero who's forced to employ a PR expert to help repair his image when
the public grows weary of all the damage he's inflicted during his lifesaving heroics.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
The agent's idea of imprisoning the antihero to make the world miss him proves successful, but
will Hancock stick to his new sense of purpose or slip back into old habits?

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
John Hancock, played by Will Smith.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Mary, played by Charlize Theron.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Ray, played by Jason Bateman.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Aaron, played by Jae Head.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Red, played by Eddie Marsan.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Man Mountain, played by David Mattey.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
Hancock is a 2008 American superhero film starring Will Smith as John Hancock, an
amnesiac, alcoholic, reckless superhuman trying to remember his past.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
The film is directed by Peter Berg and written by
Vince Gilligan and Vy Vincent Ngo.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
The film also stars Charlize Theron, Jason Bateman and Eddie Marsan.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
The story was originally written by Vy Vincent Ngo in 1996.

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
It languished in development hell for years with various directors attached, including Tony Scott, Michael Mann (who would later co-produce the
film), Jonathan Mostow and Gabriele Muccino, before being filmed in mid-2007 in Los Angeles with a production budget of $150 million.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
In the United States, the film was rated PG-13 by the Motion Picture Association of America after changes
were made at their request in order to avoid an R rating, which it had received twice before.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
Columbia Pictures released the film in theaters in
the United States on July 2, 2008.

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
While Hancock received mixed reviews from critics, who found it promising, but let down by the mid-movie change
in tone, it grossed $629.4 million worldwide, becoming the fourth highest-grossing film of 2008.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The film explores themes of love of one's life, flying,
alcohol, advertising expert, superhero.
